# AI Office frontend

Northgate Office UI for a one-person virtual company with AI employees. Separate repo from the backend — do not merge the two, and do not nest `frontend/` inside the backend repo.

- **UI:** https://ai-office.fjdresources.com
- **API:** https://api-aioffice.fjdresources.com
- **Repo:** https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-frontend
- **Backend:** https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-backend

Stack: Vite 8, React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, lucide-react. JavaScript + JSX (no TypeScript). Deployed via Docker (nginx SPA) + Coolify.

## What works today

- TOTP login + JWT auth (frontend ↔ backend, real API)
- Chat with 6 AI agents via `POST /api/message/:agentId` (real API)
- @mention hand-off between agents
- "Turn into task/project" from War Room chat (POST `/api/tasks` / `/api/projects`)
- Projects and tasks load from the API after login (empty list is valid)
- Files (`GET`/`POST` `/api/files`, JWT download) and activity (`GET /api/activity`) from the live API
- TopBar bell lists the same activity feed (empty is valid)
- Tools from `GET /api/tools`; composer Tools picker sends selected ids on chat POST
- Dark-themed, responsive UI with collapsible panels
- Dockerized frontend with nginx SPA config

## Auth and API

JWT is stored in `localStorage`. All HTTP goes through `src/api/client.js`.

Production MFA is backend Coolify **`TOTP_SECRET`** only ([ai-office-backend#15](https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-backend/issues/15)). One Base32 value (`A–Z`, `2–7`); no quotes, no `=`. Do not use `JWT_SECRET`. After changing that env var, recreate the backend container. Login 401 is not a UI bug — do not reopen #4. Smoke [#6](https://github.com/fjdresources/ai-office-frontend/issues/6) passed 2026-08-19.

Enum mapping (API `todo` / `in_progress` / `high` ↔ UI `Todo` / `In Progress` / `High`, plus `due` null ↔ `Unscheduled`) lives only in `client.js`. Views keep display labels.

| Endpoint | Method | Purpose | Helper |
|----------|--------|---------|--------|
| `/api/auth/login` | POST | TOTP → `{ token }` | `login()` |
| `/api/auth/verify` | GET | Verify JWT → `{ user }` | `verifyToken()` |
| `/api/message/:agentId` | POST | Agent chat (`tools` optional catalog ids) | `sendMessage()` |
| `/api/message/:agentId` | GET | Chat history | `getMessages()` |
| `/api/projects` | GET/POST | List / create projects | `getProjects()` / `createProject()` |
| `/api/projects/:id` | GET/PATCH/DELETE | One project | `getProject()` / `updateProject()` / `deleteProject()` |
| `/api/tasks` | GET/POST | List / create tasks | `getTasks()` / `createTask()` |
| `/api/tasks/:id` | GET/PATCH/DELETE | One task | `getTask()` / `updateTask()` / `deleteTask()` |
| `/api/files` | GET/POST | List / upload multipart `file` (max 25MB) | `getFiles()` / `uploadFile()` |
| `/api/files/:id/download` | GET | Attachment stream (JWT, not JSON) | `downloadFile()` |
| `/api/activity` | GET | Newest-first feed | `getActivity()` |
| `/api/tools` | GET | Catalog `{ tools: [{ id, name }] }` (empty is valid) | `getTools()` |

War Room uses API id `warroom` for GET and POST (history key). Backend maps that thread to the Chief of Staff model. `toApiAgentId()` is only for matching projects to a department.

`VITE_API_BASE_URL` is inlined at Vite build time (see `.env.example` and the Docker `ARG`).

`INITIAL_PROJECTS` / `INITIAL_TASKS` remain unused leftovers in `constants.js`; `App.jsx` does not import them.

## Key files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/main.jsx` | React root, StrictMode + AuthProvider |
| `src/App.jsx` | Login gate + office shell / views |
| `src/api/client.js` | Fetch wrapper, JWT, agent id mapping, project/task/file/activity/tools helpers |
| `src/context/AuthContext.jsx` | Token, verify-on-load, login/logout |
| `src/data/constants.js` | Theme `T`, agents, mock data |
| `src/components/*` | Sidebar, top bar, workspace, panels, views |
| `src/index.css` | Tailwind v4 import + full-height reset |
| `vite.config.js` | Vite 8 + React + Tailwind v4 plugins |
| `Dockerfile` / `nginx.conf` / `docker-compose.yaml` | Coolify production build |

## Deploy

Coolify resource → this repo → `docker-compose.yaml` → domain **ai-office.fjdresources.com** port **80**. Cloudflare Tunnel origin `https://localhost:443`, **No TLS Verify** on. Backend `CORS_ORIGIN` must be `https://ai-office.fjdresources.com`. Merge to `main` Auto Deploys via GitHub App webhooks (Access Bypass on `coolify.fjdresources.com/webhooks/*`; dashboard stays TOTP). Do not enable the Coolify instance API. See `git-deploy.mdc`.
